{"parentUuid":"620f8c53-b216-4b7c-9ed2-3813f4386c01","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_013jdMTSoveKU7Tz5GAneimN","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"db12c260-ff35-4af9-82a9-b5b7267e6cbe","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:55:35.801Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"db12c260-ff35-4af9-82a9-b5b7267e6cbe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyrk6B1PCs7uUQ2jFL7w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steps 1 and 2 of the corpus are pushed as 9f8c4bf. CI passes with 333 tests, and the safeguard passed after two refactors.\n\n**D61, which replaces D59's atlas:**\n- What a journey teaches about its region becomes a charter change, so the repository stays the one source of truth for the project.\n- It comes in two kinds, both under `.agents/` only:\n  - **Lesson:** anything codified. A rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or permission in `.agents/settings.json`.\n  - **Corpus entry:** the **why**: why the code is shaped this way, a surprise, a scenario. It goes in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, with `paths:` globs at the top.\n- Changes go on the journey's own branch, or on a branch of their own when a journey ends in the marsh.\n- What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database, for the learning loop on the Guide.\n\n**How the corpus loads now:**\n- **Core** (`corpus.rs`) reads an entry's `paths:` front matter and matches globs (`*` within one folder, `**` across folders). It strips the `/work/repo/` prefix and tracks which entries a turn has already been given.\n- **Server:** the corpus is read from the journey's base commit together with the charter, so an agent can't change it mid-journey.\n- **Gate:** the first time in a turn that a `sandbox::fs::*` call opens a matching path, the gate holds the call, runs it, and returns the entry in `<corpus name=\"…\">` tags ahead of the output. The entry isn't given again in that turn.\n- A new gate test checks it: the first matching read is held, a second one goes straight through, and a path that doesn't match is unaffected.\n\n**Not proven live yet:** the gate test passes, but no real journey has read a corpus file. Proving it costs one model run on a test region. I'll do that only if you say so.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- **Step 3, in the app:** signing a region note asks whether it's a lesson or a why. For a why, it asks which paths. It then commits under `.agents/` on the journey's branch. This replaces the field notes currently saved in the audit, which are now out of date under D61.\n- **Bastion notes on the Guide:** each one can become guidance or a check at its waypoint.\n- **The Map's harbor town** shows the region's lessons and corpus, read from the repository, instead of the old atlas."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":835589,"output_tokens":815,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":593,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":815,"cache_read_input_tokens":835589,"cache_creation_input_tokens":593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":593},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f8787dbe-6463-4695-a559-e4ed70de0306","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgyrk5ZJ7yCPQ5wgsHxKn","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d8e731f-f5ab-46d4-b893-8a62bf9bc22f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:55:35.796Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
