dLines":7,"newStart":87,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D58 | Nothing is global. Each rule, agent, skill, hook, reviewer and grant applies only where it is selected: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows. An item with no selection applies nowhere. A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch. Every page shows all servers or one; on All servers a row names its server, and a change goes to that server. This replaces D57's Global view with All workflows, and D53's rule that only record pages span servers. |"," | D59 | A field note is what a job taught, one sentence signed by the person who wrote it, about the workspace (the project) or about Bastion (its workflows and harness). It is an audit entry on the job, so the chain signs it and nothing rewrites it. A workspace's notes are its atlas, where the next request starts. A job that comes home, landed or in the marsh, draws its way back to the atlas. |"," | D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |","-| D61 | What a journey teaches about its region is a charter change, never a separate atlas, so each repository stays the one source of truth for its project. It is one of two kinds: a lesson (codified practice: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or a permission in `.agents/settings.json`) or a corpus entry (the why: why the code is shaped this way, a surprise, a scenario for the product, in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, whose `paths:` globs say where it is relevant). An agent is given a corpus entry only when it opens a matching path. Bastion writes charter changes only under `.agents/`, on the journey's own branch, or on a branch of its own for a journey that ends in the marsh. What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database and feeds the learning loop on the Guide. This replaces D59's atlas. |","+| D61 | What a journey teaches about its region is a charter change, never a separate atlas, so each repository stays the one source of truth for its project. It is one of two kinds: a lesson (codified practice: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or a permission in `.agents/settings.json`) or a fact (a corpus entry: the why: why the code is shaped this way, a surprise, a scenario for the product, in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, whose `paths:` globs say where it is relevant, inferred from the journey's change and the note). An agent is given a corpus entry only when it opens a matching path. Bastion writes charter changes only under `.agents/`, on the journey's own branch, or on a branch of its own for a journey that ends in the marsh. What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database and feeds the learning loop on the Guide. This replaces D59's atlas. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":301,"oldLines":12,"newStart":301,"newLines":13,"lines":[" "," Next, notes become charter changes (D61, replacing D59's atlas):"," ","-- Signing a note about the region asks which kind it is. A lesson is","-  codified: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or permission","-  in `.agents/settings.json`. The why (a reason, a surprise, a","-  scenario) goes to `.agents/corpus/<name>.md` with the paths it is about. The change is committed on the journey's","-  branch, or on a branch of its own when the journey ended in the marsh.","-- The corpus is loaded by path: when an agent opens a path a corpus","+- Done: signing a note asks its kind: a lesson, a fact, or about Bastion.","+  A lesson goes to `.agents/rules/<name>.md`; a fact goes to","+  `.agents/corpus/<name>.md` with its paths inferred from the journey's","+  change and the paths the note names. Each is committed on a branch of","+  its own for a person to merge.","+- Next: write onto the journey's own branch while it is still open.","+- Done: the corpus is loaded by path: when an agent opens a path a corpus","   entry names, it is given that entry, once per turn."," - The Map's harbor town shows the region's rules and corpus, read from","   the repository."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4edd0c9d-1804-488a-ac48-faba8b9a2962","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":1,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"266d761b-6e94-49cd-857c-6859280c33aa","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
