{"parentUuid":"59994d5c-3b8c-484b-9b37-749341e96e68","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01CV3DT2Q2DYuZKcHh2AkJ8H","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6bc0167d-a1b7-402c-8367-1d1b64fcb4dc","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:04:11.866Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"6bc0167d-a1b7-402c-8367-1d1b64fcb4dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgysQCX4fQfApNbfzvCVU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed as 51b72be. CI passes with 335 tests, and the safeguard passed after one refactor. Paths are inferred, and the kind is called **fact**.\n\n- **Signing a note** on a journey offers **A lesson**, **A fact** or **About Bastion**, each with a hint of what to write.\n  - A lesson is committed to `.agents/rules/<name>.md`.\n  - A fact is committed to `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`. Its `paths:` come from the paths the note names, plus the folder of each file the journey changed. If neither gives a path, it's relevant everywhere (`**`).\n  - Each goes on a branch of its own for you to merge. The note card shows the branch, for example \"a fact on ian/charter-…, to merge\". A note about Bastion stays in Bastion's audit.\n- **Live test** on test journey `j1c15ab9b` (region demo-gh, my scratch repository): the test fact landed in `.agents/corpus/test-fact-calcpy-keeps-one-function.md`. It inferred `paths: calc.py` from the note and was signed \"Learned on journey j1c15ab9b, signed by Ian Johnson\". `main` was unchanged. I then deleted the test branch.\n- **The words follow:** the trail's way home now ends at \"THE CHARTER\". The Map's harbor card is now \"What demo-gh has learned\", with the shelves Lessons, Facts and About Bastion.\n- **Leftovers you'll see:** my earlier test note, signed under D59, shows as \"a workspace\". It's in the audit chain, so it can't be removed.\n\n**Left on this thread:**\n1. When the journey's own branch is still open, write lessons and facts onto it. Today they always get a separate branch.\n2. Prove in a live run that a fact reaches an agent. This costs one model run on a test region.\n3. Notes about Bastion on the Guide, where each one can become guidance or a check.\n4. A lesson as a hook or permission in `.agents/settings.json`. Today a lesson is always a rule file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":792623,"output_tokens":681,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":792623,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"90d1407e-450e-4709-8146-e513ed0b06bd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgysQC42rRyA5F4oLQoCr","type":"assistant","uuid":"290ac1f2-75ea-4ea9-a5de-eff2bac76151","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:04:11.863Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
