{"parentUuid":"4c61e20d-918f-42f8-a60f-c7b340c0e939","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyvriwUsVs2ZDr4xD3WS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On the Guide, each note about Bastion now offers both guidance and a check, at the waypoint it was learned. Committed as 84fb158 and not pushed. CI passes with 342 tests, and the safeguard passed.\n\n- **Waypoint:** each note records the step its journey was at when signed. A journey that's already home records the last step it reached. Notes from before this change, and old journeys with no trail on record, apply to the trail or to every trail.\n- **Guide:** each note shows \"Guidance at Corpus check › look\" and \"A check at Corpus check › look\". The buttons use the trail's name, not its id.\n- **Check:** the form opens in place, with the call it binds (such as `sandbox::exec`) and the words the call holds. \"Add the check\" stays disabled until a call is named. The new rule is enforced at that waypoint.\n\n**Live check:**\n- A note on `j4d1075d2` got the waypoint `look`.\n- In the app, I added a check through the form. The server stored it with `function: sandbox::exec`, `contains: git push`, `rung: enforced`, `steps: [we36039fe/look]`. Then I removed it.\n- Three more test notes about Bastion are now permanent in the audit chain.\n\n**Also seen:** after the relaunch, the server switcher shows only \"local\". Server \"two\" (pid 32561, an old build) is missing, and I didn't look into why.\n\nNext in the plan is L3: make Journeys the home page, with a decisions inbox for waiting journeys, held calls and charter branches to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":245449,"output_tokens":564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":267,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":245449,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":267},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48c6c796-217f-44fd-bc2b-2c2e6cfe808f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyvriecN12qWPzzERfaE","type":"assistant","uuid":"9fba8425-99db-4b5a-b523-c13c420c0dee","timestamp":"2026-11-12T23:49:31.036Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
