{"parentUuid":"2f8c7c94-bfd7-4395-9ba1-bde6e5fad36f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01ULjM5VpMYZLQn114dRXdXn","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":63},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c3ca9477-dcef-48a3-874c-e4b1699c48e9","timestamp":"2026-11-13T00:10:39.765Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"2f8c7c94-bfd7-4395-9ba1-bde6e5fad36f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2622718c-ca77-4b9a-b6dc-4a140fe24fcf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ULjM5VpMYZLQn114dRXdXn","type":"tool_result","content":"## Agent primitives: parity with Claude Code, kept small\n\nBastion offers the primitives a coding-agent harness offers, so a team's\nsetup moves over without a rewrite.\n\n| Claude Code | Bastion | Kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Charter `AGENTS.md`, and rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Skills | Skills: a charter's `.agents/skills`, or a plugin's | Guidance |\n| Subagents | Agents: a step that runs one, or a reviewer | Guidance, Check |\n| Hooks | Hooks before a call, and when a step ends | Check |\n| Permissions: allow, ask, deny | Permissions: allowed or ask; no grant refuses | Permission |\n| MCP servers | MCP servers, as tools a permission names | Tool |\n| Plugins and marketplaces | Plugins: installed per server, then applied | Plugin |\n| Output styles | Rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Slash commands | Commands: a charter's or a plugin's, run by a prompt step | Guidance |\n\n**Plugins.** A plugin is a git repository with a manifest that lists its\nskills, agents, commands, hooks and MCP servers, as a Claude Code plugin does. A\nperson installs it on a server, from a URL or a marketplace list, at a\npinned commit. Installing it adds nothing to a job: each part shows on the\nHarness page, off, and a person applies it to steps like any other item\n(D58). Updating a plugin is a new pinned commit, so a job always records\nwhich version ran. Caveman is the first plugin to try: its skills and its\nprompt hook map onto guidance and a hook.\n\n## The look and feel: an expedition\nDECISIONS.md:26:**Non-goals for now:** a web client, managed hosting, a plugin system for\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugin hooks that need the host.** A Claude Code hook runs on the\n  person's machine; a Bastion hook runs in the job's VM. A plugin hook that\n  expects the host's files or tools may not work there.\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Codified and ambient context.** Guidance and checks are codified\n  context: written down, stable, and Bastion can scope and judge them.\n  Ambient context comes from MCP servers and other outside sources: it is\n  scattered, it changes over time, and it depends on state. How should\n  Bastion handle it: where it came from, how fresh it is, and when to read\n  it again? Today an MCP server is only a grant.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"954c598d-a614-483c-9b4b-953770cdf685","timestamp":"2026-11-13T00:10:39.902Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Agent primitives: parity with Claude Code, kept small\n\nBastion offers the primitives a coding-agent harness offers, so a team's\nsetup moves over without a rewrite.\n\n| Claude Code | Bastion | Kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Charter `AGENTS.md`, and rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Skills | Skills: a charter's `.agents/skills`, or a plugin's | Guidance |\n| Subagents | Agents: a step that runs one, or a reviewer | Guidance, Check |\n| Hooks | Hooks before a call, and when a step ends | Check |\n| Permissions: allow, ask, deny | Permissions: allowed or ask; no grant refuses | Permission |\n| MCP servers | MCP servers, as tools a permission names | Tool |\n| Plugins and marketplaces | Plugins: installed per server, then applied | Plugin |\n| Output styles | Rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Slash commands | Commands: a charter's or a plugin's, run by a prompt step | Guidance |\n\n**Plugins.** A plugin is a git repository with a manifest that lists its\nskills, agents, commands, hooks and MCP servers, as a Claude Code plugin does. A\nperson installs it on a server, from a URL or a marketplace list, at a\npinned commit. Installing it adds nothing to a job: each part shows on the\nHarness page, off, and a person applies it to steps like any other item\n(D58). Updating a plugin is a new pinned commit, so a job always records\nwhich version ran. Caveman is the first plugin to try: its skills and its\nprompt hook map onto guidance and a hook.\n\n## The look and feel: an expedition\nDECISIONS.md:26:**Non-goals for now:** a web client, managed hosting, a plugin system for\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugin hooks that need the host.** A Claude Code hook runs on the\n  person's machine; a Bastion hook runs in the job's VM. A plugin hook that\n  expects the host's files or tools may not work there.\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Codified and ambient context.** Guidance and checks are codified\n  context: written down, stable, and Bastion can scope and judge them.\n  Ambient context comes from MCP servers and other outside sources: it is\n  scattered, it changes over time, and it depends on state. How should\n  Bastion handle it: where it came from, how fresh it is, and when to read\n  it again? Today an MCP server is only a grant.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"089ee0f1-0a00-41cc-af76-22aea55b21a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2f8c7c94-bfd7-4395-9ba1-bde6e5fad36f","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.