{"parentUuid":"f2f828d8-aa45-42e4-aedb-aaf0e9ab170b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2622718c-ca77-4b9a-b6dc-4a140fe24fcf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011FejGhfipa15n6vpj7DxU8","type":"tool_result","content":"passed 349 failed 0\nM  DECISIONS.md\nM  PLAN.md\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/harness.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/mod.rs\nA  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/plugins.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/machine.rs\nA  crates/bastion-server/src/plugins.rs\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b27a2152-9efc-449f-bc65-1812e0a93983","timestamp":"2026-11-13T00:16:14.499Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"passed 349 failed 0\nM  DECISIONS.md\nM  PLAN.md\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/harness.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/mod.rs\nA  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/plugins.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/machine.rs\nA  crates/bastion-server/src/plugins.rs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":88,"oldLines":6,"newStart":88,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D59 | A field note is what a job taught, one sentence signed by the person who wrote it, about the workspace (the project) or about Bastion (its workflows and harness). It is an audit entry on the job, so the chain signs it and nothing rewrites it. A workspace's notes are its atlas, where the next request starts. A job that comes home, landed or in the marsh, draws its way back to the atlas. |"," | D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |"," | D61 | What a journey teaches about its region is a charter change, never a separate atlas, so each repository stays the one source of truth for its project. It is one of two kinds: a lesson (codified practice: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or a permission in `.agents/settings.json`) or a fact (a corpus entry: the why: why the code is shaped this way, a surprise, a scenario for the product, in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, whose `paths:` globs say where it is relevant, inferred from the journey's change and the note). An agent is given a corpus entry only when it opens a matching path. Bastion writes charter changes only under `.agents/`. A note signed while the journey is under way is written onto the journey's own branch before any step that reaches past its VM (so a pull request carries it) and again as it lands, with paths inferred from its change outside `.agents/`; a file already written as it would be is left alone; a note signed after the journey came home goes on a branch of its own. What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database and feeds the learning loop on the Guide. This replaces D59's atlas. |","+| D62 | A plugin is a git repository laid out as a Claude Code plugin, installed on one server from an `https://` URL at a pinned commit. It lives as its own checkout under the server's data folder, detached at that commit, so the checkout is the record and moving it to a new commit is a new install. Its parts (skills, agents, commands, hooks and MCP servers, from the manifest or their usual files) are listed on the Guide, off: installing one adds nothing to a journey until a person applies a part (D58). Plugin parts are data that map onto Bastion's own kinds, so this is not the code-defined guard plugin system the non-goals rule out. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":294,"oldLines":8,"newStart":294,"newLines":13,"lines":[" "," ### L7. Plugins"," ","-- Install a plugin from a git URL at a pinned commit, on one server. Its","-  skills, agents, commands, hooks and MCP servers show on Harness, off.","+- Done (D62): install a plugin from an https git URL at a pinned commit,","+  on one server. Its skills, agents, commands, hooks and MCP servers show","+  on the Guide, off. Tried live with caveman at 9b68f7e.","+- Next: apply a part at a scope: its files go into the job's VM, a skill","+  or a command runs as a step, an agent as a step or a reviewer, a hook","+  as a hook. Hooks that expect the host (`node`, `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT`)","+  are the open question below."," - Each job records the plugin commits it ran with."," "," ### L8. First run"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d845025f-6613-459c-8c43-0c160836e401","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":7,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2f828d8-aa45-42e4-aedb-aaf0e9ab170b","session_id":"4fe5